  "category": "Dynamic Programming",
  "statement": "The Fibonacci numbers, commonly denoted `F(n)`, form a sequence such that each number is the sum of the two preceding ones, starting from 0 and 1:\n`F(0) = 0`, `F(1) = 1`\n`F(n) = F(n - 1) + F(n - 2)`, for `n > 1`.\n\nGiven `n`, calculate `F(n)`.",
  "constraints": [
    "0 <= n <= 35"
  ],
  "function_name": "fib",
  "starter_code": "def fib(n: int) -> int:\n    # Implement your solution below\n    pass\n",
  "reference_solution": "def fib(n: int) -> int:\n    if n <= 1:\n        return n\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b\n",
